; exit 127 (see .exit)
; The facts an error-propagating loop stands on. They pull in different
; directions - one is about where the RECURSION sits, one about where
; the ERROR VALUE sits, and one was a cost nothing reclaimed until
; 2026-08-25.
;
; Measured 2026-08-16, before `docs/error-model.md` specified anything,
; because a propagation model that cannot survive a loop is not a model.
;
; 1. WHERE THE RECURSION SITS. `(match (recur ...) ...)` is not a tail
;    call - the match is what the call returns INTO - so the loop
;    conversion does not fire and each step costs a frame. Measured at
;    32 bytes of stack per frame: that shape survives 250,000
;    iterations and dies of SIGSEGV at 262,144, which is 8 MiB exactly.
;    The shape below is the other one: the fallible call is the
;    SCRUTINEE and the recursion is what the `Good` arm ANSWERS, so the
;    self call is in tail position inside the arm and converts.
;    1,000,000 iterations here, four times past the cliff.
;
;    This is the happy direction, and it decides the surface: a
;    propagation form desugars to `(match e ((Bad ..) ..) ((Good x)
;    BODY))` with the continuation in the ARM, which is the shape that
;    converts. Writing it the other way round is what does not work.
;
; 2. WHERE THE ERROR VALUE SITS. The tail-call release boundary
;    (MM-LIFE-2c event 4) releases a reference parameter across the
;    jump, and a `data` block births owned at count 1. Constructed
;    INLINE in the tail-call argument the boundary retain takes it to 2
;    and the single release returns it to 1 - never 0, so it never
;    files. Bound to a `let` first, the frame's scope release spends the
;    birth count and the loop is flat. Measured over 2000 iterations
;    each carrying a fresh 32-byte String: inline 288,176 bytes,
;    returned from a function 288,176, let-bound 176.
;
;    Term 4 asserts this over a POLYMORPHIC error type applied at
;    concrete arguments, because that is what a `Result` is and because
;    `fldClass` classifies an applied type by its head - a monomorphic
;    probe would not have asked the question.
;
; 3. WHAT THE FALLIBLE CALL COSTS - 32 bytes until 2026-08-25, and
;    zero since. The block a fallible call RETURNS used to be
;    reclaimed under no spelling: matching the call directly and
;    let-binding it first both leaked exactly 32 bytes per call - one
;    `Res` block - measured at 10,000 and 50,000 iterations, both
;    32.0 bytes/iter on the nose. This section said then that "a
;    fixture asserting the leak would have to be rewritten the day it
;    is fixed", and term 32 is that rewrite.
;
;    What held the block was the BINDER. A `match` scrutinee is
;    released after the merge only when no arm's binder escapes
;    through that arm's body (`scrutineeReleasable`), and a binder
;    reaching its arm's value read as an escape whatever its type -
;    so `((Good v) v)` kept the block alive to protect an `Int`.
;    The field-read path never had this problem, because a field read
;    still names its field and `fieldReadIsScalar` can classify it;
;    by the time the escape walk reaches an arm, the field has become
;    a bare variable with nothing on it to classify. The checker now
;    stamps each pattern binder with the type it resolved
;    (`stampPatBinderTy`), and it stamps the INSTANTIATED one, which
;    is the half a declared-type test could not reach: `Good`'s field
;    is declared `a`, and only this match site knows this `Good` came
;    out of a `(Res Int Int)`.
;
;    Term 8 stays exactly as it was - the same loop with no `Res` in
;    it - because it is what attributes a difference to the error
;    value rather than to the loop. But two flat lines cannot tell
;    reclamation from a blind instrument, so term 64 is the other
;    half: the ablation this file has named since 2026-08-16 - drop
;    `carry`'s `let` and construct the error inline - measured by the
;    same probe pair, and REQUIRED to grow. If the instrument stops
;    seeing allocation, term 64 goes to 0 and this fixture fails.
;    `docs/error-model.md` ERR-MEM-4 records the whole measurement.
;
;    NO PROBE HERE USES A `memAlloc` DELTA ANY MORE, and the reason is
;    that one of them went green on linux-x86_64 while leaking. Every
;    probe used to bracket its loop with two `memAlloc` addresses,
;    which is sound only while the bump stays inside one chunk. Term
;    32's ABLATED arm leaks 640,032 bytes, and 640 KB is enough to
;    cross one: the two addresses then live in unrelated chunks, the
;    subtraction answers a number about nothing, and on Linux that
;    number came back UNDER the 4096 gap. So the term PASSED on a
;    compiler with the defect fully present, while darwin-aarch64
;    failed it correctly. A crossing made the check pass instead of
;    fail, which is worse than no check at all.
;
;    Fixing term 32 alone would have been the smaller lie. Term 64
;    crossed a chunk on the very next run - its delta came back
;    **-144**, a negative number of bytes - and it had been green on
;    darwin only by where the boundary happened to fall. Terms 4 and 8
;    assert FLATNESS through the same instrument and carry the same
;    hazard by construction: a crossing is only reachable when the arm
;    allocates heavily, which is exactly when the term should fail.
;
;    So all four read the arena MARK CELL, as `372-arc-owned-results`
;    does: word 0 is the bump, word 2 is the chunk. The three FLAT
;    terms (4, 8, 32) require the chunk to be unchanged AND the bump
;    to have barely moved, so a crossing is a failure. Term 64 asserts
;    GROWTH, so for it a crossing IS the growth and satisfies the term
;    on its own. Each direction fails the way an unmeasurable
;    measurement has to.
;
;    That measurement also fixed the metric. A `memAlloc` address delta
;    is only meaningful BELOW the allocator's chunk size: the same
;    loop read 32.0 bytes/iter at 10,000 and 50,000 and 795.7 at
;    100,000, because at ~3.2 MB the bump crossed into a chunk that is
;    not contiguous with the last and the raw subtraction counted the
;    gap. Every delta below stays well under it.
;
;   64  the instrument can SEE growth: 2000 Strings allocated and KEPT
;       move the same probe pair past the gap the flat terms sit under
;   32  the block a fallible call answers IS reclaimed, matched
;       directly and let-bound alike - 10,000 iterations of each
;   16  the arm-tail propagation loop completes 1,000,000 iterations
;    8  the same loop with no Result in it allocates nothing
;    4  a reference-carrying error value, let-bound at the boundary, is
;       reclaimed - 2000 iterations, each allocating a fresh String
;    2  an error answers unchanged through the loop it exits
;    1  every step above ran
;
; Ablations, run 2026-08-16. Move the recursion into the scrutinee:
; SIGSEGV and no exit code at all, which is why term 16 is a completion
; and not a value. Drop the `let` in `carry` and construct the error
; inline: term 4 goes to 0 and that bump moved 288,176. RE-MEASURED
; 2026-08-25 it moves 144 over the same 2000 iterations, so that
; spelling is no longer an ablation of anything and term 64 uses a
; retained allocation instead - see the note on `hoard`.
;
; Ablation for term 32, run 2026-08-25: make `binderIsScalar` in
; `self_host/codegen.ax` answer 0 unconditionally - one word - and the
; bump over those 20,000 iterations moves 640,000 bytes, 32 per call,
; exactly as it did before the fix. `scripts/check-fallible-reclaim.sh`
; runs that ablation rather than describing it.
(import Str)

(import Mem)

(import Vec)

(data Res (a e)
  (Good a)
  (Bad e))

(:: b2i (-> Bool Int))

(fn (b2i x)
  (if x
    1
    0
  )
)

(:: wide (-> Int String))

(fn (wide k) (strDup "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"))

; a fallible step that does not, in fact, fail here
(:: step (-> Int (Res Int Int)))

(fn (step n)
  (if (< n 0)
    (Bad n)
    (Good 1)
  )
)

; the same step with no error value, for term 8's control
(:: stepPlain (-> Int Int))

(fn (stepPlain n) 1)

; THE SHAPE. The fallible call is the scrutinee; the recursion is the
; Good arm's answer, in tail position, and converts to a loop.
(:: total (-> Int Int (Res Int Int)))

(fn (total n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    (Good acc)
    (match (step n)
      ((Bad e) (Bad e))
      ((Good v) (total (- n 1) (+ acc v)))
    )
  )
)

; term 8's control: identical loop, no Res constructed
(:: totalPlain (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (totalPlain n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    acc
    (totalPlain (- n 1) (+ acc (stepPlain n)))
  )
)

; a loop carrying a reference in the error payload, let-bound so the
; frame may release it
(:: carry (-> (Res Int String) Int Int))

(fn (carry r n)
  (if (<= n 0)
    0
    (let ((next (Bad (wide n))))
      (carry next (- n 1))
    )
  )
)

; Term 64: the probe pair is not blind. 2000 Strings allocated and
; KEPT - the Vec outlives the second probe, so nothing may reclaim
; them - must read as growth. Without this, terms 4, 8 and 32 are
; three flat lines with no evidence that a line which SHOULD move
; would.
;
; It is here because the ablation this file named for six weeks - drop
; `carry`'s `let` and construct the error inline - stopped being one.
; Re-measured 2026-08-25: that spelling moves the bump 144 bytes over
; 2000 iterations, not the 288,176 recorded on 2026-08-16, so it is a
; flat line too now and would have made a control that cannot fail.
; A control has to be something the allocator must answer for.
(:: hoard (-> Int (Vec String)))

(fn (hoard n)
  (let (
    (v vecNewRef)
    (mut i 0)
  )
    {
      (while (< i n)
        {
          (vecPush v (wide i))
          (set i (+ i 1))
        })
      v
    }
  )
)

; ERR-MEM-4's two spellings. The recursion is the tail call in both -
; the `match` sits inside an ARGUMENT to it, so term 1's cliff is not
; in play and what these measure is the `Res` block alone. `v` is an
; `Int` living in a field the declaration spells `a`.
(:: drain (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (drain n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    acc
    (drain
      (- n 1)      (+
        acc        (match (step n)
          ((Good v) v)
          ((Bad e) 0)
        )
      )
    )
  )
)

(:: drainLet (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (drainLet n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    acc
    (drainLet
      (- n 1)      (+
        acc        (let ((r (step n)))
          (match r
            ((Good v) v)
            ((Bad e) 0)
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )
)

; an error raised mid-loop must answer unchanged, not be re-wrapped
(:: failAt (-> Int Int (Res Int Int)))

(fn (failAt n acc)
  (if (== n 0)
    (Good acc)
    (match (if (== n 500)
      (Bad 77)
      (Good 1)
    )
      ((Bad e) (Bad e))
      ((Good v) (failAt (- n 1) (+ acc v)))
    )
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (let (
    (mut acc 0)
    (mut steps 0)
  )
    {
      (set acc (+
        acc        (*
          16          (b2i
            (==
              (match (total 1000000 0)
                ((Good x) x)
                ((Bad e) (- 0 1))
              )              1000000
            )
          )
        )
      ))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      (let ((a1 __axiom_arena_mark))
        {
          (totalPlain 100000 0)
          (let ((a2 __axiom_arena_mark))
            (set acc (+
              acc              (*
                8                (b2i (&&
                  (== (__load64 a2 2) (__load64 a1 2))                  (< (- (__load64 a2 0) (__load64 a1 0)) 4096)
                ))
              )
            ))
          )
          (set steps (+ steps 1))
        }
      )
      (let ((b1 __axiom_arena_mark))
        {
          (carry (Bad (wide 0)) 2000)
          (let ((b2 __axiom_arena_mark))
            (set acc (+
              acc              (*
                4                (b2i (&&
                  (== (__load64 b2 2) (__load64 b1 2))                  (< (- (__load64 b2 0) (__load64 b1 0)) 4096)
                ))
              )
            ))
          )
          (set steps (+ steps 1))
        }
      )
      (let ((c1 __axiom_arena_mark))
        {
          (drain 10000 0)
          (drainLet 10000 0)
          (let ((c2 __axiom_arena_mark))
            (set acc (+
              acc              (*
                32                (b2i (&&
                  (== (__load64 c2 2) (__load64 c1 2))                  (< (- (__load64 c2 0) (__load64 c1 0)) 4096)
                ))
              )
            ))
          )
          (set steps (+ steps 1))
        }
      )
      (let ((d1 __axiom_arena_mark))
        (let ((h (hoard 2000)))
          {
            (let ((d2 __axiom_arena_mark))
              (set acc (+
                acc                (*
                  64                  (b2i (&&
                    (== (vecLen h) 2000)                    (||
                      (!= (__load64 d2 2) (__load64 d1 2))                      (> (- (__load64 d2 0) (__load64 d1 0)) 4096)
                    )
                  ))
                )
              ))
            )
            (set steps (+ steps 1))
          }
        )
      )
      (set acc (+
        acc        (*
          2          (b2i
            (==
              (match (failAt 1000 0)
                ((Good x) x)
                ((Bad e) e)
              )              77
            )
          )
        )
      ))
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      (if (== steps 6)
        (+ acc 1)
        acc
      )
    }
  )
)
